00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:14.660
Each year, various marketing firms assemble
highly-publicized lists of the “Most valuable

00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:16.750
brands in the world”.

00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:22.770
This one, Brandz, considers financial factors
— such as how much revenue a company generates,

00:00:22.770 --> 00:00:28.450
as well as subjective measures, like awareness
and opinion surveys of the general, consumer

00:00:28.450 --> 00:00:29.839
public.

00:00:29.839 --> 00:00:34.579
Last year’s rankings, for example, went
pretty much as you’d expect.

00:00:34.579 --> 00:00:38.660
At the top are Amazon, Apple, Microsoft, and
Google.

00:00:38.660 --> 00:00:45.130
Below them are other iconic, global brands
like Disney, Starbucks, and Netflix.

00:00:45.130 --> 00:00:48.340
But a few, in particular, stand out.

00:00:48.340 --> 00:00:53.489
While they’ve scored very highly precisely
for their popularity, strangely, there’s

00:00:53.489 --> 00:00:56.829
a very good chance you’ve never heard of
them.

00:00:56.829 --> 00:01:02.960
One such company is Tencent — whose Twitter
account has a measly 23,000 followers.

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:09.590
Visa, meanwhile, despite being a credit card
company, has 383,000.

00:01:09.590 --> 00:01:12.910
Mastercard has 480,000.

00:01:12.910 --> 00:01:18.220
Of course, “Number of Twitter followers”
is by no means a complete or accurate picture

00:01:18.220 --> 00:01:24.160
of a company’s popularity, but that’s
exactly the point: Tencent is one of the world’s

00:01:24.160 --> 00:01:30.690
most recognizable brands, and yet most of
the world doesn’t even know what it is.

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:34.650
Such is the insularity of the Chinese market.

00:01:34.650 --> 00:01:39.190
There are, however, many good reasons to become
familiar.

00:01:39.190 --> 00:01:44.750
At the highest level, Tencent is one of the
three Chinese internet giants — along with

00:01:44.750 --> 00:01:49.290
Baidu and Alibaba — together abbreviated
as “BAT”.

00:01:49.290 --> 00:01:54.680
Headquartered in an unusually-shaped building
in Shenzhen, across the border from Hong Kong,

00:01:54.680 --> 00:02:00.920
the company exists in a Chinese mirror-image
of Silicon Valley — with arduous work hours,

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:06.430
an intense culture of competition, and a reputation
for doing the unconventional.

00:02:06.430 --> 00:02:12.110
Tencent was founded, most famously, by “Pony”
— his nickname — Ma, whose first major

00:02:12.110 --> 00:02:18.250
success was “QQ” — a social network
which took off in early-internet China.

00:02:18.250 --> 00:02:23.810
In many ways, Ma, and Tencent were simply
in “the right place at the right time”.

00:02:23.810 --> 00:02:30.030
But two of its ideas stand out, if not for
their originality, certainly for their early

00:02:30.030 --> 00:02:31.040
application.

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:37.860
Firstly, rather than rely on advertising for
the majority of its revenue, QQ helped pioneer

00:02:37.860 --> 00:02:40.000
“Value Added Services”.

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:46.600
Users could purchase virtual “goods” like
customizable avatars, gifts, and status symbols.

00:02:46.600 --> 00:02:52.240
Secondly, with each subsequent product, Tencent
never truly started from scratch.

00:02:52.240 --> 00:02:57.470
It would carry its enormous and ever-growing
user base from one venture to the next until

00:02:57.470 --> 00:03:02.060
it had near monopoly-level control over the
world’s largest market.

00:03:02.060 --> 00:03:08.319
In 2011, it launched what became its most
popular app ever: the chat application known

00:03:08.319 --> 00:03:12.819
in English as WeChat, which integrated with
QQ.

00:03:12.819 --> 00:03:18.760
Its momentum grew dramatically with the introduction
of the now-ubiquitous WeChat Pay and Mini

00:03:18.760 --> 00:03:24.970
Programs, which allows users to install other
apps within the app — bypassing the App

00:03:24.970 --> 00:03:30.610
Store and iOS’ rules — which Apple conveniently
turns a blind eye to.

00:03:30.610 --> 00:03:36.530
Today, WeChat is called a “super-app”
or the “operating system of China” because

00:03:36.530 --> 00:03:42.430
of its ability to do everything from act as
a wallet, pay rent, shop online, and much

00:03:42.430 --> 00:03:44.020
much more.

00:03:44.020 --> 00:03:50.930
Its over 1.2 billion users spend 4 hours a
day in the app, on average in China.

00:03:50.930 --> 00:03:56.620
That’s more than American users spend on
all social media, combined.

00:03:56.620 --> 00:04:02.810
With WeChat, Tencent is like Amazon in that
it acts as a gatekeeper of the market — setting

00:04:02.810 --> 00:04:09.290
prices, copying and killing competitors, and
effectively taxing all other companies.

00:04:09.290 --> 00:04:15.620
When foreign firms enter China, they inevitably
partner with Tencent or die of obscurity.

00:04:15.620 --> 00:04:21.889
And yet the app is only a relatively small
part of the Tencent business empire.

00:04:21.889 --> 00:04:28.510
Its seven divisions each compare favorably,
if not embarrass, entire other companies.

00:04:28.510 --> 00:04:33.090
For example, its payment services division
is almost as large as Paypal.

00:04:33.090 --> 00:04:37.300
It’s subscription revenue closely follows
that of Netflix.

00:04:37.300 --> 00:04:41.520
And it makes more from games than Sony or
Nintendo.

00:04:41.520 --> 00:04:48.419
Outside of China, Tencent holds a vast collection
of investments, including Tesla, Snap, and

00:04:48.419 --> 00:04:52.270
Epic Games — the maker of Fortnite and the
Unreal Engine.

00:04:52.270 --> 00:04:56.840
It also wholly owns Riot Games, the parent
of League of Legends.

00:04:56.840 --> 00:05:03.050
Tencent’s game store, called WeGame, is
significantly bigger than Steam, its American

00:05:03.050 --> 00:05:04.350
competitor.

00:05:04.350 --> 00:05:10.190
You could say that Tencent is not a games
company, but it is the world’s largest game

00:05:10.190 --> 00:05:11.770
company.

00:05:11.770 --> 00:05:15.210
That is also one of its most long-standing
criticisms.

00:05:15.210 --> 00:05:20.180
That somewhere along the evolution from chat
application to internet technology social

00:05:20.180 --> 00:05:25.810
network, game, payment service platform, the
company lost its soul.

00:05:25.810 --> 00:05:32.610
Some argue it lacks a singular drive, motivation,
or focus, and is more akin to a boring old

00:05:32.610 --> 00:05:34.330
investment fund.

00:05:34.330 --> 00:05:40.270
Tencent is a part-owner of so many hundreds
of companies, you’ve almost certainly unknowingly

00:05:40.270 --> 00:05:42.790
used one of its products.

00:05:42.790 --> 00:05:45.520
But you might ask: Why?

00:05:45.520 --> 00:05:51.210
Any country with China’s diversity of regions,
languages, and cultures, not to mention its

00:05:51.210 --> 00:05:56.280
sheer size — would seem to predispose it
to much competition.

00:05:56.280 --> 00:06:02.640
Why is the U.S. home to Facebook, Twitter,
Netflix, Discord, Instagram, and YouTube — while

00:06:02.640 --> 00:06:08.870
China, four times its size, home to effectively
one company to rule them all?

00:06:08.870 --> 00:06:14.910
The answer is counterintuitive to almost everything
most people have been taught about China.

00:06:14.910 --> 00:06:16.040
In a word: non-interference.

00:06:16.040 --> 00:06:23.600
It’s not exactly true that the Chinese government
is overbearing and controlling.

00:06:23.600 --> 00:06:26.510
For foreign companies, absolutely.

00:06:26.510 --> 00:06:32.940
But in terms of oversight and industry regulation,
China has actually given certain companies

00:06:32.940 --> 00:06:35.229
extraordinary freedom.

00:06:35.229 --> 00:06:41.940
The very existence of Alibaba, Baidu, and
Tencent prove China’s willingness to tolerate

00:06:41.940 --> 00:06:45.950
extreme monopolies when it benefits the state.

00:06:45.950 --> 00:06:51.199
Broadly speaking, large private Chinese corporations
serve three purposes:

00:06:51.199 --> 00:06:57.740
Firstly, they elevate the image of Chinese
entrepreneurship, and therefore, the “China

00:06:57.740 --> 00:06:59.370
brand” more generally.

00:06:59.370 --> 00:07:05.530
Evidence of its transformation into a “Moderately
prosperous society”, in party speak.

00:07:05.530 --> 00:07:11.650
Second, the success of domestic companies
comes at the expense of foreign ones.

00:07:11.650 --> 00:07:17.479
To the very limited extent that Western companies
succeed in China, they do so with the express

00:07:17.479 --> 00:07:22.120
approval and financial benefit of a Chinese
counterpart.

00:07:22.120 --> 00:07:27.380
This is even legally codified, in the way
that foreign firms are required by law to

00:07:27.380 --> 00:07:29.620
partner with a local one.

00:07:29.620 --> 00:07:35.820
Third, finally, and most controversially,
global brands provide China with extra-territorial

00:07:35.820 --> 00:07:37.070
power.

00:07:37.070 --> 00:07:44.010
By holding majority or even minor stakes in
overseas companies, China can impose its laws

00:07:44.010 --> 00:07:47.530
and sensibilities on the rest of the world.

00:07:47.530 --> 00:07:53.430
When overseas Chinese communities get their
news from WeChat, they continue, for example,

00:07:53.430 --> 00:07:59.520
to be shaped by Chinese narratives, despite
living on Australian, Canadian or American

00:07:59.520 --> 00:08:00.650
soil.

00:08:00.650 --> 00:08:06.199
Tencent is so colossally huge thanks to China’s
grand political ambitions.

00:08:06.199 --> 00:08:11.729
But, now, having accomplished them, the mood
is changing.

00:08:11.729 --> 00:08:16.930
And no recent event better represents this
shift than the cancellation of the Ant Group

00:08:16.930 --> 00:08:18.389
IPO.

00:08:18.389 --> 00:08:23.639
According to reports, Chairman Xi Jinping
himself, stopped one of the largest Chinese

00:08:23.639 --> 00:08:29.320
financial firms from going public — sending
a clear message that no company, interest

00:08:29.320 --> 00:08:36.349
or individual, even the very richest and most
influential, is above the law or party.

